# Next.js Architecture Rules

## Server vs Client Components

### Server Components (Default)
- Pages in `app/` are server components by default
- Can use Node.js APIs (`fs`, `path`, etc.)
- Can directly access database/filesystem
- Cannot use React hooks or browser APIs
- Use `async/await` for data fetching

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Server Component
import { getServerTranslations } from '@/lib/i18n/server'
import { getAllPosts } from '@/lib/blog' // Uses 'fs' module

export default async function BlogPage() {
  const { locale, translations } = await getServerTranslations()
  const posts = getAllPosts(locale)
  return <div>...</div>
}
```

### Client Components
- Mark with `'use client'` directive at top
- Can use React hooks (useState, useEffect, etc.)
- Can access browser APIs (localStorage, window, etc.)
- **CANNOT import server-only modules** (`fs`, `path`, etc.)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Client Component
'use client'

import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'
import { getUserProgress } from '@/lib/progress-tracker' // Pure client-side

export default function ProgressTracker() {
  const [progress, setProgress] = useState(null)
  
  useEffect(() => {
    setProgress(getUserProgress())
  }, [])
  
  return <div>...</div>
}
```

### Critical Error to Avoid

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Importing server modules in client component
'use client'

import { getAllPosts } from '@/lib/blog' // ERROR: Uses 'fs' module!

// ✅ GOOD - Pass data as props from server component
'use client'

interface Props {
  posts: BlogPost[] // Data from server
}

export default function ClientList({ posts }: Props) {
  return <div>...</div>
}
```

## Hydration Errors

### Prevent Server/Client Mismatch

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Causes hydration error
'use client'

export default function Component() {
  const data = localStorage.getItem('key') // Available on client, not server
  return <div>{data}</div> // Mismatch!
}

// ✅ GOOD - Wait for client mount
'use client'

export default function Component() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null)
  
  useEffect(() => {
    setData(localStorage.getItem('key'))
  }, [])
  
  if (!data) return null // Return null during server render
  return <div>{data}</div>
}
```

## File Organization

```
app/
  page.tsx              # Server component (default)
  blog/
    page.tsx            # Server component
    ClientList.tsx      # Client component (pass data as props)
  
lib/
  blog.ts               # Server-side (uses fs/path)
  progress-tracker.ts   # Client-side (uses localStorage)
  
components/
  ui/                   # Can be server or client
  blog/
    BlogCard.tsx        # Server component (no interactivity)
    BlogList.tsx        # Server component
```
